<title>USA: Union Pacific sets price for rail co's notes.</title>
<headline>Union Pacific sets price for rail co's notes.</headline>
<dateline>BETHLEHEM, Pa. 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Pacific Corp said it will purchase the 9-3/8 percent senior notes due 2005 of Southern Pacific Rail Corp at a price equal to $1,086.84 per $1,000 principal amount plus accrued interest.</p>
<p>The interest would accrue up to but not including the payment date, which is assumed to be October 7, the company said.</p>
<p>The offer is currently scheduled to expire at midnight EDT on October 2.  </p>
<p>As part of the previously announced merger of the two companies, Union Pacific said it would buy any and all of the outstanding $375 million in principal of Southern Pacific's senior notes.</p>
</text>
